#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bessel_k_scaled

#% text
# `bessel_k_scaled(nu, x)` gives e^x K_nu(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Machine values are computed without forming K_nu(x), so they do not underflow at large x: ratios such as K_1/K_2 at x = 800 stay finite.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bessel_k_scaled(1, 2.0)
#% output
#= 1.0334768470686886

#% text
# A ratio at large x:

#% cell
bessel_k_scaled(1, 800.0)/bessel_k_scaled(2, 800.0)
#% output
#= 0.9981279260279697

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bessel_k`, `bessel_i_scaled`
